body:
`fieldOptions` passes through Object field types (e.g. `currency`, `percent`, etc.), but `FilterBuilder` only switches on `text | number | boolean | date | select`. This will cause numeric/date fields to get the wrong operator set and input type. Consider normalizing ObjectUI field types to the FilterBuilder types when building `fieldOptions` (e.g. `currency`→`number`, `datetime`→`date`).
```suggestion
        return Object.entries(objectDef.fields).map(([key, field]: [string, any]) => {
            const rawType = (field?.type as string | undefined)?.toLowerCase();

            let normalizedType: 'text' | 'number' | 'boolean' | 'date' | 'select';

            // Map common Object field types to FilterBuilder's limited type set
            if (
                rawType === 'integer' ||
                rawType === 'int' ||
                rawType === 'float' ||
                rawType === 'double' ||
                rawType === 'number' ||
                rawType === 'currency' ||
                rawType === 'money' ||
                rawType === 'percent' ||
                rawType === 'rating'
            ) {
                normalizedType = 'number';
            } else if (
                rawType === 'date' ||
                rawType === 'datetime' ||
                rawType === 'datetime_tz' ||
                rawType === 'timestamp'
            ) {
                normalizedType = 'date';
            } else if (
                rawType === 'boolean' ||
                rawType === 'bool' ||
                rawType === 'checkbox' ||
                rawType === 'switch'
            ) {
                normalizedType = 'boolean';
            } else if (
                rawType === 'select' ||
                rawType === 'picklist' ||
                rawType === 'single_select' ||
                rawType === 'multi_select' ||
                rawType === 'enum' ||
                // Heuristic: fields with discrete choices behave like selects
                Array.isArray(field?.options?.choices) ||
                Array.isArray(field?.options?.options)
            ) {
                normalizedType = 'select';
            } else {
                normalizedType = 'text';
            }

            return {
                value: key,
                label: field.label || key,
                type: normalizedType,
                options: field.options,
            };
        });
```
